{"name":"Bologna Sausage","hex":"#ffcfdc","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bologna","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A seasoned Italian sausage made from beef, pork or veal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of baloney (“nonsense”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bologna"},{"term":"sausage","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food made of ground meat (or meat substitute) and seasoning, packed in a section of the animal's intestine, or in a similarly cylindrical shaped synthetic casing.","An individual item of this food."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To squeeze (something) tightly into in a rolled or sausage-like form.","To squeeze (something) into something tightly fitting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sausage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bologna sausage","blocks":[{"text":"Bologna sausage, informally Baloney, is an American cooked sausage. It derives from Italian mortadella Bologna PGI, a variety of mortadella, a large salume. Its seasonings include black pepper, nutmeg, allspice, celery seed, coriander, and myrtle berries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Lyoner-1.jpg/330px-Lyoner-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bologna_sausage","wikidata":"Q543025"},{"title":"Bologna","blocks":[{"text":"Bologna is the capital and largest city of the Emilia-Romagna region in northern Italy. It is the seventh most populous city in Italy, with 391,473 inhabitants from 150 different nationalities. Its metropolitan province is home to more than 1 million people as of 2026. Bologna is most famous for being the home to the oldest university in continuous operation, the University of Bologna, established in AD 1088."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Torri_di_Bologna%2C_Bologna.jpg/330px-Torri_di_Bologna%2C_Bologna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o